{"status":"completed","summary":"Restored `branch_ledger` on node1 and configured node2 as its persistent read-only MySQL 5.7 replica. Original rows 1001/1002 remain unchanged. Test commits replicated normally, including across a deliberate disconnect and both sequential node reboots. Final state is six unique rows totaling 166.87, with matching source/replica positions and zero replication errors.","actions_performed":["Installed Ubuntu 16.04-compatible MySQL 5.7.33 without changing the OS release or 4.4 kernel.","Enabled row-based binary logging on node1 and relay-log recovery plus read-only protections on node2.","Created a node2-restricted account with only `REPLICATION SLAVE`.","Preserved the staged export unchanged at `/srv/legacy2/mysql-replication-catchup/ledger.sql`.","Demonstrated normal replication, direct-write rejection, disconnect/catch-up, and post-reboot replication.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Restore the ledger while retaining original IDs and amounts","command_ids":["cmd-a9ebcd42b65b4e31","cmd-38d7012a32d143d8"],"summary":"Node1 contains original rows 1001=12.50 and 1002=-3.25, plus committed replication-test rows; all six IDs are unique."},{"requirement":"Use a replication-only account and keep node1 as writer","command_ids":["cmd-a9ebcd42b65b4e31","cmd-2e5be131e151489a","cmd-38d7012a32d143d8","cmd-8b9732849b514c20"],"summary":"`ledger_repl` has only `REPLICATION SLAVE`; node1 is writable while node2 has read-only and super-read-only enabled and rejects direct inserts."},{"requirement":"Committed inserts arrive on node2","command_ids":["cmd-681243d9f2044175","cmd-2e5be131e151489a","cmd-fe0dacacfa974c29","cmd-8b9732849b514c20"],"summary":"Commits before and after the reboot sequence reached node2; final source and replica coordinates both equal mysql-bin.000002:439."},{"requirement":"Catch up after a short disconnect without loss or duplication",